      <span class="callout-icon">⚠</span>
      <div><strong>The parental cover decision:</strong> 40% of claims on ESCP (employee + spouse + children + parents) policies are for parents — and parents generate the highest average claim at ₹73,000. Removing parental cover to cut costs results in considerable out-of-pocket spending for employees. The recommended approach is to introduce voluntary parental cover (employee-funded, employer-facilitated) rather than removing it entirely — less expensive than a default ESCP plan, more comprehensive than a retail policy the employee would buy independently.</div>
